Z||000000||triker||05-23-2000||06:38 PM||||I've asked for help on here a couple of times with my WOT shift probs and questions about the built in rev limiter in the earlier ECM's.  Well after hooking up a tach, I found that the limiter is working fine at exactly 6,000 rpm's and I was still in 2nd gear.  After some head scratching I went back to my trusted tranny specialist and asked him if reducing my 2700 hundred pound car to a 1500 pound trike would affect the shift timing.  "But of course!"  Now I have to start playing with springs and weights in the governer. WML  Triker||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||05-24-2000||10:25 AM||||I don't buy that.<P>I think you have either a problem with the TV cable and valve or you have a governer with some crap in it. Both are known problems that will cause late or no up shifting. There are GM TSB on both problems. Find someone that will let you dig in their Alldata software or get the pop mechanics personal version of alldata and get the TSB upgrade.<P>The problem with the TV valve requires you to make a minor alteration to the valve body divider plate. in this problem one whole in the plate isn't quite big enough and sometimes the valve can't properly follow the throttle.<P>Problem with the governor is just that. Dirt in the valve blocking it up. The TSB for this tells you how to make a little screen to prevent it.||||reg||1
